# Layout and UX/UI (law)

General UX/UI principles **MUST** be followed **at all costs**. A control that works but looks unfinished is a **bug**.

Canonical: `AIRULES/00-AGENT-CONTRACT.md` §2f, `AIRULES/05-VIEWS-TEMPLATES-ASSETS.md` §8c–§8e, `AIRULES/33-DACORE-PAGES-AND-UI.md` §6–§6b.

**Admin forms (MUST):** numbered section + one-sentence lede + tinted Why-this-matters when the cluster is not obvious. **MUST NOT** one wall of inputs. Chrome stays in **this** module — do not copy another module’s namespaced chrome. Compact: `23-admin-page-sections.mdc`.

## When adding a button (MUST, every time)

1. Check **padding on all sides** — left, right, **top**, and **bottom**. It **MUST NOT** sit flush against the parent (card, `card-body`, footer, modal, drawer, page).
2. **Last in the block:** if the buttons are the **last content** of that block, **almost always** add space **below** (`card-footer` + `pb-3`/`pb-4`, or CSS `padding-bottom`). Dropping Save at the bottom with no bottom padding is the most common layout bug.
3. Place it **deliberately vs the parent**: centered or the same rhythm as sibling cards — not shoved left.
4. If you zero one side (`pt-0`, `border-0`), **compensate** the other (`pb-4` or CSS `padding-bottom`).
5. Desktop **and** mobile: touch target, wrap, no overflow.

## Fail now

- Save/primary glued to the card or page edge
- Buttons last in a card/`card-body`/modal with **no** padding below
- Uncentered or cramped vs sibling footers
- Claiming done from the PHP handler without reading the HTML/CSS chrome
- Opening a live browser to “check padding” unless the user asked (`AIRULES/00` §2r) — read the layouts instead
